xFusionCorp Industries — ML Platform Docker CI Pipeline
This project provides a fully automated, four-stage shell-based Docker CI/CD pipeline (build.sh) designed for the fraud-detection Flask microservice. The pipeline standardizes automated testing, image construction, semantic tagging via Git short SHAs, and secure artifact publishing to a local private registry.

📁 Repository Layout
Plaintext
/root/code/ci/
├── app/
│   ├── app.py             # Flask application exposing /health and /predict endpoints (Port 8086)
│   ├── test_app.py        # Pytest test suite covering health checks and fraud classification flows
│   ├── Dockerfile         # Python 3.11-slim container specification
│   └── .git/              # Initialized local Git repository with baseline commit history
└── build.sh               # Automated end-to-end CI/CD script
🚀 Pipeline Execution Flow (build.sh)
The script executes four consecutive stages under strict error handling (set -euo pipefail):

Test Stage: Discovers and runs pytest across the app/ directory to validate service behavior prior to containerization.

Build Stage: Compiles the local container image (ml-ci-app:latest) using the isolated app/ build context.

Tag Stage: Dynamically extracts the active short Git SHA via git -C app rev-parse --short HEAD and applies tags for the local private registry (localhost:5555).

Push Stage: Publishes both the unique SHA-tagged artifact and the latest reference to the local registry:2 instance.

🛠️ Complete build.sh Implementation
Bash
#!/bin/bash
# Shell-based CI pipeline for the ml-ci-app image.
#
# Stages: test -> build -> tag (git SHA) -> push to local registry.
# Run from /root/code/ci/.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"

IMAGE="ml-ci-app"
REGISTRY="localhost:5555"

# --- Stage 1: test
echo "[ci] stage 1/4 — running tests"
python3 -m pytest app/

# --- Stage 2: build
echo "[ci] stage 2/4 — building image"
docker build -t "$IMAGE:latest" app/

# --- Stage 3: tag
echo "[ci] stage 3/4 — tagging"
SHA=$(git -C app rev-parse --short HEAD)
TAGGED="$REGISTRY/$IMAGE:$SHA"
docker tag "$IMAGE:latest" "$TAGGED"
docker tag "$IMAGE:latest" "$REGISTRY/$IMAGE:latest"

# --- Stage 4: push
echo "[ci] stage 4/4 — pushing"
docker push "$TAGGED"
docker push "$REGISTRY/$IMAGE:latest"

echo "[ci] complete: $TAGGED"
